WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.634 --> 00:00:01.634
-Wiz!

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.901
-What up, baby?
-Welcome back.

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:04.701
You know, you've performed here
many times.

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:06.300
We've played games.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.267
You're one of the greatest
guests we've ever had.

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:09.734
-Yeah, I always have fun here.

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:10.934
-But we've never had a chat.

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:12.501
We've never talked to each other
on the couch.

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:14.501
-Oh, not on the couch.
-So, I'm happy that you're here.

00:00:14.501 --> 00:00:17.033
I want to get to know you and
talk to you about everything.

00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:19.334
I know Salma Hayek Pinault
was just out here.

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:20.467
-Mm-hmm.
-And we learned

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:22.300
on "The Masked Singer"...
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.100
-...that was your
first celebrity crush.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.968
Here's you, by the way...
-Yeah.

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:27.133
-...on "The Masked Singer."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:29.067
-Yeah, yo.
[ Laughs ]

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:31.567
-Any certain movie from Salma?

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:33.767
-"Dusk Till Dawn" was one of
my favorite ones.

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:36.434
And then, when she was in
"Desperado," as well.

00:00:36.434 --> 00:00:38.000
-Oh, she just crushes, right?
-Yeah, she --

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.100
-Did you get say hi?
-Yeah, I got to say hi.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.234
-You did?
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:43.167
-Okay. That's what
I'm talking about, right?

00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:44.634
[ Laughter ]
-It was awesome.

00:00:44.634 --> 00:00:46.901
'Cause, like, she ate somebody
in "Dusk Till Dawn,"

00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:48.267
so she didn't eat me
in real life.

00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:49.901
-No, yeah, you didn't --
She didn't --

00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:51.334
She didn't do it.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:52.834
You have a hobby of yours

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:54.434
that I wanted to ask you
a question about.

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:56.200
I follow you on the socials.
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.534
-And this is you, and you said
you "Made a banger tonight,"

00:00:58.534 --> 00:01:00.234
which I'm assuming
you recorded a song.

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:01.601
-Yep.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.601 --> 00:01:04.901
-You said, "About to watch ASMR
and catch some zzz's."

00:01:04.901 --> 00:01:07.267
-Yep, yep.
-So, you watch --

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:10.000
ASMR is -- that's,
like, when people go

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.167
up to the microphone
and make noises.

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:12.934
-Yeah, it's really,
really soothing.

00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:15.234
Like, everybody
has their own triggers.

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:17.601
And I got my own triggers,
as well, so, yeah.

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:20.067
-What is your --
what's your best --

00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:21.901
what's the --
-I like hair noises.

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:23.901
Like, I like getting
my hair played with.

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:25.667
So, I just watch --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:27.367
-People like it, too.
Apparently, it's a thing.

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:28.501
[ Laughter, scattered cheers ]

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:29.901
I didn't know the audience
was into this.

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:32.167
-Yeah, I watch people play with,
like, mannequins and, like,

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:34.634
just rub their hair and part it
and all that stuff.

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:36.067
[ Laughter ]
It's soothing.

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:37.367
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:38.667
-That's soothing right there.

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:40.267
So, you got someone playing
with a mannequin head?

00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:41.434
-Yeah, yep.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:42.667
-And you go right --
you go right to sleep?

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:44.167
-I'm asleep in three minutes.

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:46.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:49.868
-I love that.

00:01:49.868 --> 00:01:52.968
You made news
a couple weeks ago, buddy,

00:01:52.968 --> 00:01:57.033
when you said that you
smoked weed with Michael Phelps.

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:58.400
-Yeah, that was awesome.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:01.667
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:02:01.667 --> 00:02:04.734
-I mean, he's an Olympian.
He's a gold medalist.

00:02:04.734 --> 00:02:06.234
He is the best swimmer in the --

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:07.734
You said that
he had Aquaman lungs.

00:02:07.734 --> 00:02:09.167
-Yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:11.601
I think he might've had
better lungs than Aquaman, bro.

00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:12.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.601 --> 00:02:13.968
-Really?
-Champion, bro.

00:02:13.968 --> 00:02:15.801
-Yeah, but what
made you go, like,

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.567
"Oh, he's got Aquaman lungs?"
I mean, he just --

00:02:17.567 --> 00:02:21.968
-Because the way -- he hit the
joint a little bit differently.

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:24.367
He hit it like --
like a gold medalist would.

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:29.100
-Really?
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.200
Did he just, like,
inhale the whole thing?

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.834
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:34.167
It disappeared after --
-It disappeared.

00:02:34.167 --> 00:02:35.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:37.267
He just kept inhaling, and then
he just sucked it all in there.

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:38.367
You're like, "Wow."
And then he exhaled

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:40.634
and went back in your hand?
Yeah.

00:02:40.634 --> 00:02:42.334
But you have your own line
of stuff, right?

00:02:42.334 --> 00:02:43.934
-Yeah, yeah.
It's called Khalifa Kush.

00:02:43.934 --> 00:02:45.267
-Khalifa Kush?
-Uh-huh.

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:47.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.033
-And did he handle
the Khalifa Kush?

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:50.400
Could he handle it?
-Yeah, he did.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.901
Anybody can handle
the Khalifa Kush.

00:02:52.901 --> 00:02:55.767
I recommend it for non-smokers,
first-time smokers,

00:02:55.767 --> 00:02:57.133
or O.G. smokers.

00:02:57.133 --> 00:02:58.601
We got flower, we got vapes,

00:02:58.601 --> 00:03:01.701
we got edibles
in all select markets.

00:03:01.701 --> 00:03:04.567
We're available in Michigan,
Pennsylvania, Maryland,

00:03:04.567 --> 00:03:06.667
Florida, Arizona.

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:09.968
And we just released
another strain.

00:03:09.968 --> 00:03:11.334
It's called Khalifa Mints.

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:13.033
It's Khalifa Kush
mixed with menthol,

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:15.267
and we've got more strands
coming out next year, as well.

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:16.534
-Gosh.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:16.534 --> 00:03:18.200
-Yeah!
-Crushing it, buddy.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.801
Crushing it.
-And I smoked K.K.

00:03:19.801 --> 00:03:21.300
before I said that.
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.968
-Oh, my God.

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:24.267
Look at this guy.

00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:26.100
Can you explain who this guy is?
That's you.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.400
-Yeah, that's me.
-Yeah.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:28.767
Now, what are you doing here?
You're in a movie?

00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:31.067
-Yeah, I'm playing
George Clinton.

00:03:31.067 --> 00:03:32.534
Yeah, yeah.
-I love George Clinton.

00:03:32.534 --> 00:03:33.801
Look at this.
-Yeah, yep.

00:03:33.801 --> 00:03:35.067
-That's the real George Clinton.
-Parliament Funk-- yeah.

00:03:35.067 --> 00:03:36.601
-Come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:39.200
-Dr. Funkenstein.
-Dr. Funkenstein.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.567
"Spinning Gold."

00:03:40.567 --> 00:03:43.701
Is it tough to play somebody
who is alive?

00:03:43.701 --> 00:03:44.734
Did you talk to George?

00:03:44.734 --> 00:03:45.901
-Yeah, we -- I talked to him.

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:47.901
His grandkids
were actually on set, too.

00:03:47.901 --> 00:03:50.367
So, it was really cool to, like,
vibe off of them and just hear,

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:52.367
you know, stories or...
-Oh, my gosh.

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:54.334
-...even just them telling me,
like, how proud he would be,

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:56.501
like, you know,
seeing me do the role.

00:03:56.501 --> 00:03:58.033
So it was official.
It was fun.

00:03:58.033 --> 00:03:59.467
-That's pretty cool.
-Yeah, it was cool.

00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:01.334
-I'm looking forward to that.
That's coming out next year.

00:04:01.334 --> 00:04:02.534
-Yeah, I am, too.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:02.534 --> 00:04:04.000
-Let's talk about
the new album, bud.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.334
-Yes, sir, yes, sir.
-It's out.

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:07.367
"Multiverse."
-Uh-huh.

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:09.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:12.834
-They love it.

00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:14.734
"Multiverse" has nothing to do
with Marvel, by the way.

00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:16.000
-No.
-No.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:19.000
This is -- This is like
"Multiverse" because --

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.968
-It's like the multi--

00:04:20.968 --> 00:04:23.501
It's like finding myself
in different dimensions.

00:04:23.501 --> 00:04:25.200
Or just taking you
on a journey with me.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.701
-Yeah.
-Yeah, yep.

00:04:26.701 --> 00:04:29.601
-Because I was thinking, like,
maybe because you're versatile.

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:31.334
-Yeah, very versatile.
Exactly.

00:04:31.334 --> 00:04:34.267
I don't like to do
one style of music,

00:04:34.267 --> 00:04:36.968
so I want to create
an experience for people

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:38.968
that they can just have from me,
you know?

00:04:38.968 --> 00:04:40.334
-Is there any music
you don't like?

00:04:40.334 --> 00:04:43.667
-No, I love all music.
I love pop, rock, country,

00:04:43.667 --> 00:04:45.367
reggae, funk --
-You like country?

00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:47.000
-Yeah, I love country.
-Yeah.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:48.167 --> 00:04:50.501
And you like country
'cause of the lyrics?

00:04:50.501 --> 00:04:52.400
-Yeah, I like the writing, like,

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.367
how it just invites you
into the song.

00:04:54.367 --> 00:04:56.634
Like, before
the second verse is over,

00:04:56.634 --> 00:04:57.767
you know how to sing
the whole song.

00:04:57.767 --> 00:04:58.901
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.901 --> 00:05:00.501
There is an art to that.
-It's really clever.

00:05:00.501 --> 00:05:02.667
-There is an art to that.
-Yeah, I love that.

00:05:02.667 --> 00:05:04.501
-You started rapping
when you were 9 years old.

00:05:04.501 --> 00:05:06.868
-Uh-huh.
-Now you have a son who is 9.

00:05:06.868 --> 00:05:09.467
-Yep, Sebastian.
-And how's Bash?

00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:11.767
-He's really good, man.
He's a genius.

00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:13.300
There's times
where I leave the house,

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.133
and I'll come back home,
he's like, "Hold on, Dad.

00:05:15.133 --> 00:05:16.634
I'm recording my song
right now."

00:05:16.634 --> 00:05:18.767
He's, like, in the studio,
already doing his thing.

00:05:18.767 --> 00:05:20.300
-He's in the studio?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:21.400
-I thought you were gonna say
he's in his bedroom.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:22.868
-No, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.868 --> 00:05:24.501
I have a studio --
I have a studio in the house.

00:05:24.501 --> 00:05:27.133
So, he goes in there, and
he bosses my engineer around.

00:05:27.133 --> 00:05:29.234
And he's cool as heck, yo.
-Wow.

00:05:29.234 --> 00:05:30.634
-It's really cool to see.
-So, we have to look forward

00:05:30.634 --> 00:05:32.968
to your son maybe coming --
-For sure.

00:05:32.968 --> 00:05:34.467
-Yeah?
-He'll be on the couch next.

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:35.834
-That's what
I'm talking about, yeah.

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:37.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:37.501 --> 00:05:40.667
Wiz, Wiz Khalifa, you're
performing for us tonight.

00:05:40.667 --> 00:05:42.567
What song are you gonna do
for us tonight?

00:05:42.567 --> 00:05:43.934
-I'm gonna be doing
"Memory Lane."

00:05:43.934 --> 00:05:45.767
-"Memory Lane."
That's what I'm talking about.

00:05:45.767 --> 00:05:47.234
Wiz Khalifa, everybody!

00:05:47.234 --> 00:05:49.033
"Multiverse" is out now.

00:05:49.033 --> 00:05:51.968
"Memory Lane" when we come back.
Stick around, everybody.

